{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "Total Victory: World Conflict 1939-1945",
    "steam_appid": 3359110,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Total Victory</strong> is a World War 2 military simulation wargame based on history. It blends realistic data with practical play creating a moderately complex game that focused on depth of strategy to win. Play any of the major powers during that time period.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Uses a modified Mercator map and a tile system for an elegant readable map</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Production uses ore into industry that creates material from factories</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Automated supply system of ports and sources along routes that adds another level of strategic play.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each hex holds 1 land, 1 naval, and 1 air counter</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u00a0 Land counters can hold up to 6 units</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u00a0 Air counters can hold up to 4 units</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u00a0 Naval counters at sea can hold up to 6 units, unlimited in port</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Single capital ships researched with historical data</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u00a0 3 levels of research for each type of new ship</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Research new units, improvements in combat, and intelligence with 23 research slots</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Colorful silhouettes for infantry, tanks, and ships unique for each nation</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Total Victory</strong> is a World War 2 military simulation wargame based on history. It blends realistic data with practical play creating a moderately complex game that focused on depth of strategy to win. Play any of the major powers during that time period.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Uses a modified Mercator map and a tile system for an elegant readable map</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Production uses ore into industry that creates material from factories</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Automated supply system of ports and sources along routes that adds another level of strategic play.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each hex holds 1 land, 1 naval, and 1 air counter</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u00a0 Land counters can hold up to 6 units</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u00a0 Air counters can hold up to 4 units</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u00a0 Naval counters at sea can hold up to 6 units, unlimited in port</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Single capital ships researched with historical data</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u00a0 3 levels of research for each type of new ship</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Research new units, improvements in combat, and intelligence with 23 research slots</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Colorful silhouettes for infantry, tanks, and ships unique for each nation</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "short_description": "Take command of one or several nations during World War 2 from Europe to the Pacific. Command their economy, leaders, research, armies, air forces, and navies. Configure your armies and air groups with named divisions and individual capital ships. Relive all of World War 2.",
